,title,link,text,language,family
0,Toto language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toto_language,"Toto (Bengali: টোটো, Toto: 𞊒𞊪𞊒𞊪) is a Sino-Tibetan language spoken on the border of India and Bhutan by the Toto people. The Toto are an Indigenous community originating from Totopara, West Bengal along the border with Bhutan.",Toto,Sino-Tibetan
1,Music of Tibet - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Tibet,"The soundtrack to Kundun, by Philip Glass, has helped to popularize Tibetan music. Foreign styles of popular music have also had a major impact within the Tibetan diaspora, where Indian ghazal and filmi are very popular and American rock has produced the India-based Rangzen Shonu.",Toto,Sino-Tibetan
